# Local development only. Copy to `.dev.vars`, which is gitignored.
#
# In production none of these live in a file: each is a Worker secret, set
# with `wrangler secret put NAME` (and `scripts/setup.sh` prompts for the
# ones your chosen connector and sinks declare). The names here are the ones
# `murmur.config.ts` refers to via `{ env: 'NAME' }` — change them there and
# change them here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# Signs session tokens. At least 32 bytes; `setup.sh` generates one.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
MURMUR_SECRET=dev-secret-please-replace-at-least-32-bytes

# "1" prints structured, PII-free events to the console. Off in production.
MURMUR_LOG=1

# ------------------------------------------------- one per connector in use

# Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Used by `connector: { type: 'gemini', options: { apiKey: { env: 'GEMINI_API_KEY' } } }`
# The File Search store name is not a secret and goes in murmur.config.ts.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Retell — https://dashboard.retellai.com
# Only the key is a secret. `agentId` is per-site configuration and belongs
# in murmur.config.ts: one deployment can serve several sites, each talking
# to a different agent, so it cannot be a single environment variable.
# RETELL_API_KEY=key_...

# Any OpenAI-compatible provider reuses the `openai` connector with its own
# `baseUrl`, so give its key whatever name you reference in the config.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# Turnstile's server-side secret. The site key is public and goes in
# murmur.config.ts under `security.captcha`; this one never leaves the Worker.
#
# For local development, pair Cloudflare's always-passing test keys instead of
# registering localhost on your real widget:
#   site key  1x00000000000000000000AA
#   secret    1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_TEST_SECRET=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=0x4AAA...

# Where leads are forwarded. A webhook URL with a GUID in it is a credential —
# anyone holding it can post leads into your automation — so the real one goes
# in .dev.vars, never here.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://automation.example.com/webhook/<your-id>

# Sent as the `api_key` request header so the receiver can tell your Worker
# apart from anyone who has guessed the URL above. It must match the value in
# the receiver's own check — in n8n, the Webhook node's Header Auth
# credential, whose Name must be `api_key` and whose Value is this. A
# mismatch answers 403 "Authorization data is wrong!" and runs nothing.
#
# Referenced from murmur.config.ts as
# `headers: { api_key: { env: 'LEAD_WEBHOOK_API_KEY' } }`, so the key never
# enters that file or the deployed Worker bundle.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_API_KEY=a-shared-secret
